    "id": "lambdatest/agent-skills/agent-testing-checks-skill",
    "name": "agent-testing-checks-skill",
    "description": "Coverage checklist and review rules for testing an AI agent: a chatbot, support assistant, voice agent or tool-calling agent. Covers what to test (grounding, tool calls, side effects, multi-turn, prompt injection, data handling), how to assert on non-deterministic output, and how to read results. Use when the user asks \"how do I test my agent\", \"what should we test before launching the chatbot\", \"agent testing\", \"LLM evals\", or mentions hallucination, \"prompt injection\", red teaming or non-deterministic output. Points to Rook to generate scenarios, run the agent and grade the evidence; install rook-skill to drive Rook.\n",
